{%- comment -%}
  Renders: Arabic-only @font-face rules for Almarai (400 / 700 / 800).

  Why: the Almarai files served by Shopify's font library (almarai_n4/n7/n8) are
  Latin-only subsets with no Arabic glyphs, so Arabic text fell back to system fonts
  (e.g. Times New Roman) even though the computed font-family was Almarai.

  How: these faces join the existing "Almarai" family declared by css-variables.liquid.
  Their unicode-range covers only the Arabic blocks present in the files, so Arabic
  characters use these files and Latin characters keep using Shopify's files.
  A file is only downloaded when a page renders Arabic text at that weight.

  Files: assets/almarai-arabic-{400,700,800}.woff2 — Google Fonts Almarai v19, Arabic
  subset (fonts.gstatic.com). SIL Open Font License 1.1, no Reserved Font Name;
  see licenses/Almarai-OFL.txt.

  Usage: {% render 'ayum-arabic-font-face' %} in layout/theme.liquid, after css-variables.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- style -%}
  @font-face {
    font-family: Almarai;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url({{ 'almarai-arabic-400.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0600-06FF, U+FB50-FDFF, U+FE70-FEFF;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: Almarai;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url({{ 'almarai-arabic-700.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0600-06FF, U+FB50-FDFF, U+FE70-FEFF;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: Almarai;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url({{ 'almarai-arabic-800.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0600-06FF, U+FB50-FDFF, U+FE70-FEFF;
  }
{%- endstyle -%}
